# FTP Protocol Client Request Templates

For the FTP protocol, the client request templates include all the common FTP commands. Here are the main ones:

```
FTP: {
    "USER": ["USER <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "PASS": ["PASS <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "CWD": ["CWD <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "PWD": ["PWD\r\n"],
    "LIST": ["LIST <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "RETR": ["RETR <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "STOR": ["STOR <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "DELE": ["DELE <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "QUIT": ["QUIT\r\n"],
    "TYPE": ["TYPE <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "PASV": ["PASV\r\n"],
    "PORT": ["PORT <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "RMD": ["RMD <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "MKD": ["MKD <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "RNFR": ["RNFR <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "RNTO": ["RNTO <<VALUE>>\r\n"],
    "SYST": ["SYST\r\n"],
    "NOOP": ["NOOP\r\n"],
    "FEAT": ["FEAT\r\n"],
    "SIZE": ["SIZE <<VALUE>>\r\n"]
}
```

## Common FTP Commands

| Command | Description | Example |
|---------|-------------|---------|
| USER | Username | `USER anonymous\r\n` |
| PASS | Password | `PASS user@example.com\r\n` |
| LIST | List directory | `LIST -la\r\n` |
| RETR | Download file | `RETR filename.txt\r\n` |
| STOR | Upload file | `STOR upload.txt\r\n` |
| CWD | Change directory | `CWD /public\r\n` |
| PWD | Print working directory | `PWD\r\n` |
| DELE | Delete file | `DELE unwanted.txt\r\n` |
| QUIT | Disconnect | `QUIT\r\n` |

All FTP commands follow the same format: **Command + optional parameters + \r\n**
